# `npx vercel` uploads the working directory and does not read .gitignore.
# Without this file a CLI deploy would ship .env (API keys) and any
# service-account key in the tree. Production secrets live only in the
# Vercel project's environment variables (DEPLOYMENT.md §3).

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
serviceAccountKey.json
*serviceAccountKey*.json
*service-account*.json
*service_account*.json
*-firebase-adminsdk-*.json
*credentials*.json
*.pem
*.key
*.p8
*.pfx
*.p12
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# --- Local build output: Vercel builds its own dist ---------------------------
dist
dist-electron
dist-ssr
release
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
tsc_output.txt

# --- Emulator data and logs ---------------------------------------------------
.firebase
emulator-data
firebase-export-*
*.log
